{
  "title": "Shoulder Arthrodesis",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/shoulder-and-elbow/3128/shoulder-arthrodesis",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 5 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Introduction",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The goal of shoulder arthrodesis is **to provide a stable base** for the upper extremity optimizing hand and elbow function",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "it remains an important treatment option in appropriately selected patients",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Indications",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**stabilization of paralytic disorders**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "brachial plexus palsy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "irreparable deltoid and rotator cuff deficiency with arthropathy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "salvage of a failed total shoulder arthroplasty",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "reconstruction after tumor resection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "painful ankylosis after chronic infection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "recurrent shoulder instability which has failed previous repair attempts",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "paralytic disorders in infancy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Contraindications",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "ipsilateral elbow arthrodesis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "contralateral shoulder arthrodesis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "lack of functional scapulothoracic motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "trapezius, levator scapulae, or serratus anterior paralysis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Charcot arthropathy during acute inflammatory stage (Eichenholtz 0-2)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "elderly patients",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "progressive neurologic disease",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Glenohumeral articulation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "a relatively small amount of surface area exists allowing for predictable fusion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "to increase the available fusion area, decortication of both the **glenohumeral articular surface and the articulation between the humeral head and the undersurface of the acromion** is performed",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "only the glenoid fossa and base of the coracoid provide sufficient strength for fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**specific to the underlying condition** necessitating arthrodesis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "symptomatic dysfunction of the glenohumeral joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**AP, lateral, and axillary** views to assess bone stock available for fusion and deformities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "better to evaluate **glenoid bone loss** especially in the setting of failed arthroplasty",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "EMG",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indicated when the **neurologic condition of the scapular muscles** is ill-defined",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Surgical Technique",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Approach",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**S-shaped skin incision** beginning over the scapular spine, traversing anteriorly over the acromion, and extending down the anterolateral aspect of the arm",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Fusion position",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "goal is to allow patients to reach their mouths for feeding",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3128/images/shoulder%20arthodesis.jpg",
                  "caption": "Shows the fusion position for shoulder arthrodesis"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "think **\"30°-30°-30°\"**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "20°-30° of **abduction**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "20°-30° of **forward flexion**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "20°-30° of **internal rotation**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Technique",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rotator cuff is resected from the proximal humerus and the biceps tendon is tenodesed",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "glenoid and humeral head articular surfaces and the undersurface of the acromion are decorticated",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "arm is placed into the position of fusion (30°-30°-30°)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "a **10-hole, 4.5 mm pelvic reconstruction plate** is contoured along the spine of the scapula, over the acromion, and down the shaft of the humerus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "compression screws are placed through the plate across the glenohumeral articular surface into the glenoid fossa",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "the plate is anchored to the scapular spine with a screw into the base of the coracoid",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Postoperative care",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "a **thermoplastic orthosis** is applied the day after surgery and is maintained for 6 weeks",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "at 6 weeks, may transition to a **sling** if there are no radiographic signs of loosening",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "at 3 months, **mobilization exercises and thoracoscapular strengthening** are commenced if no radiographic signs of loosening are present",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "expected recovery period is 6-12 months",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Infection**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Nonunion**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Malposition**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Prominent hardware**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Humeral shaft fracture**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
